            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-78408",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "util-linux: util-linux: nsenter --join-cgroup leaks root cgroup migration authority"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The nsenter --join-cgroup option opens the target cgroup.procs file as root and leaves that file descriptor open across later namespace and credential changes and across execve(). Because the kernel checks later cgroup migrations using the credentials from the original open, a program run in an attacker-controlled target can inherit root's ability to move host processes between cgroups. After a privileged operator uses --join-cgroup against that target, an unprivileged user can migrate and terminate unrelated root processes."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-78408",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-78408\nSeverity: HIGH\nPackage: libuuid1\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-78408](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-78408)\nThe nsenter --join-cgroup option opens the target cgroup.procs file as root and leaves that file descriptor open across later namespace and credential changes and across execve(). Because the kernel checks later cgroup migrations using the credentials from the original open, a program run in an attacker-controlled target can inherit root's ability to move host processes between cgroups. After a privileged operator uses --join-cgroup against that target, an unprivileged user can migrate and terminate unrelated root processes.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-78408**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|HIGH|libuuid1||[CVE-2026-78408](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-78408)|\n\nThe nsenter --join-cgroup option opens the target cgroup.procs file as root and leaves that file descriptor open across later namespace and credential changes and across execve(). Because the kernel checks later cgroup migrations using the credentials from the original open, a program run in an attacker-controlled target can inherit root's ability to move host processes between cgroups. After a privileged operator uses --join-cgroup against that target, an unprivileged user can migrate and terminate unrelated root processes."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "8.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "HIGH"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-78409",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "util-linux: util-linux: X-mount.subdir detached-tree resolution can escape via intermediate symlinks"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The X-mount.subdir option uses a detached-tree fast path on Linux 6.15 and later and passes the configured subdirectory to open_tree() with AT_SYMLINK_NOFOLLOW. That flag does not stop intermediate symlink traversal or keep resolution inside the newly mounted filesystem. A local unprivileged user with an fstab-authorized X-mount.subdir entry can attach a host path at the intended mountpoint."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-78409",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-78409\nSeverity: HIGH\nPackage: libuuid1\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-78409](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-78409)\nThe X-mount.subdir option uses a detached-tree fast path on Linux 6.15 and later and passes the configured subdirectory to open_tree() with AT_SYMLINK_NOFOLLOW. That flag does not stop intermediate symlink traversal or keep resolution inside the newly mounted filesystem. A local unprivileged user with an fstab-authorized X-mount.subdir entry can attach a host path at the intended mountpoint.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-78409**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|HIGH|libuuid1||[CVE-2026-78409](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-78409)|\n\nThe X-mount.subdir option uses a detached-tree fast path on Linux 6.15 and later and passes the configured subdirectory to open_tree() with AT_SYMLINK_NOFOLLOW. That flag does not stop intermediate symlink traversal or keep resolution inside the newly mounted filesystem. A local unprivileged user with an fstab-authorized X-mount.subdir entry can attach a host path at the intended mountpoint."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "8.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "HIGH"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-78410",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "util-linux: util-linux: restricted bind mounts do not pin the source, allowing X-mount.owner/group/mode redirection"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A flaw was found in util-linux. Restricted bind mounts take the source path from fstab but do not pin that source before the privileged mount. A local unprivileged user who can replace the authorized source or a writable ancestor can redirect SUID mount(8) to bind another host directory. If the fstab entry also sets X-mount.owner, X-mount.group, or X-mount.mode, root then changes ownership or mode on that redirected inode."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-78410",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-78410\nSeverity: HIGH\nPackage: libuuid1\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-78410](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-78410)\nA flaw was found in util-linux. Restricted bind mounts take the source path from fstab but do not pin that source before the privileged mount. A local unprivileged user who can replace the authorized source or a writable ancestor can redirect SUID mount(8) to bind another host directory. If the fstab entry also sets X-mount.owner, X-mount.group, or X-mount.mode, root then changes ownership or mode on that redirected inode.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-78410**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|HIGH|libuuid1||[CVE-2026-78410](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-78410)|\n\nA flaw was found in util-linux. Restricted bind mounts take the source path from fstab but do not pin that source before the privileged mount. A local unprivileged user who can replace the authorized source or a writable ancestor can redirect SUID mount(8) to bind another host directory. If the fstab entry also sets X-mount.owner, X-mount.group, or X-mount.mode, root then changes ownership or mode on that redirected inode."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "8.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "HIGH"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-3184",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "util-linux: util-linux: Access control bypass due to improper hostname canonicalization"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A flaw was found in util-linux. Improper hostname canonicalization in the `login(1)` utility, when invoked with the `-h` option, can modify the supplied remote hostname before setting `PAM_RHOST`. A remote attacker could exploit this by providing a specially crafted hostname, potentially bypassing host-based Pluggable Authentication Modules (PAM) access control rules that rely on fully qualified domain names. This could lead to unauthorized access."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-3184",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-3184\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: libuuid1\nFixed Version: \nLink: [CVE-2026-3184](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-3184)\nA flaw was found in util-linux. Improper hostname canonicalization in the `login(1)` utility, when invoked with the `-h` option, can modify the supplied remote hostname before setting `PAM_RHOST`. A remote attacker could exploit this by providing a specially crafted hostname, potentially bypassing host-based Pluggable Authentication Modules (PAM) access control rules that rely on fully qualified domain names. This could lead to unauthorized access.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-3184**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|libuuid1||[CVE-2026-3184](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-3184)|\n\nA flaw was found in util-linux. Improper hostname canonicalization in the `login(1)` utility, when invoked with the `-h` option, can modify the supplied remote hostname before setting `PAM_RHOST`. A remote attacker could exploit this by providing a specially crafted hostname, potentially bypassing host-based Pluggable Authentication Modules (PAM) access control rules that rely on fully qualified domain names. This could lead to unauthorized access."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv3_baseScore": 5.3,
                "cvssv3_vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:L/A:N",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "5.3",
                "tags": [
